<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="014" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-02: server-side custom XML part GUID stamp (forward-only)</title>
    <phase>1 Foundation</phase>
    <gate>012 complete — the identity resolver must exist so the stamp has a fallback to complement, not replace</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New BFF surface modifying .cs in `Sprk.Bff.Api`, on the save path, writing into .docx bytes. Tags include bff-api. Code-review plus adr-check run at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Touching OOXML bytes on a save path is the highest-consequence category in this repo — ADR-049's amendment history exists because two prior approaches to .docx mutation each produced a distinct data-fidelity failure. A malformed stamp corrupts a user's work product, and the corruption may not surface until the file is opened in Word.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1-b</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>012</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ooxml, docx, save-path, dataverse, integration-test, backend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>On every Spaarke save, write the `sprk_document` GUID into a custom XML part inside the UPLOADED BYTES on the server — never by mutating the user's open document, which would dirty it and prompt an unexpected save. A stamped document that is downloaded and later re-uploaded self-identifies without a Graph round-trip. The stamp is forward-only: existing stored bytes are never rewritten.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in OOXML package structure (custom XML parts, `[Content_Types].xml`, relationship parts), .NET stream handling on a save path, and BFF service composition. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>The BFF save path stamps the `sprk_document` GUID into a custom XML part in the uploaded .docx bytes before they reach SPE. A document downloaded after a Spaarke save carries the stamp and self-identifies on re-upload. A document saved BEFORE this release is untouched and still resolves through task 012's Graph path. The user's open document in Word is never modified.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      spec.md FR-02 plus its Assumptions section: "FR-02 stamping is server-side, into the uploaded bytes — not client-side into the open document. Client-side stamping would dirty the user's document and prompt an unexpected save."
      Owner decision recorded in `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/CLAUDE.md` Decisions (2026-09-04): **FR-02 stamping is forward-only** — no retroactive rewrite of existing `sprk_document` bytes. Rationale: FR-01's Graph plus alternate-key path already identifies pre-existing Spaarke documents; the stamp is a fallback for round-tripped files; retroactive stamping would mean rewriting stored bytes for every existing document. This closes the spec's open question at line 283.
      The stamp complements task 012, it does not replace it. Identity resolution order after both ship: read the stamp if present (no Graph call), else fall back to the URL-to-Graph-to-alternate-key path.
      Residual risk accepted by the owner: a Spaarke GUID travels inside documents sent to opposing counsel. Mitigations (customer-facing documentation, or a strip-on-export option) are explicitly NOT built in r1.
      Coordination: `spaarkeai-compose-r8` owns the OTHER .docx write path and is `parallel-safe:false` across the Compose spine (plan.md §5 hot-path coordination, risk R-5). ADR-049 governs that path and must be read before touching any .docx bytes.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeCreateOnSavePromoter.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/FileAccessEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/IGenericEntityService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/014-xml-part-stamp-decisions.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="012" status="pending">The document-identity resolver — the stamp is the round-trip fallback for the Graph path 012 establishes, and the two must agree on what identity means</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the entire stamping mechanism. MUST NOT mutate the user's OPEN document in Word. No client-side custom-XML-part write, no `Office.context.document.customXmlParts` write, no round-trip that dirties the document and prompts an unexpected save. The stamp goes into the bytes already in flight to the server.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: existing stored documents. FORWARD-ONLY — no retroactive rewrite of any existing `sprk_document`'s stored bytes (owner decision 2026-09-04, project CLAUDE.md Decisions). Do not add a backfill job, a migration, or an opportunistic "stamp on next read". A document saved before this release stays unstamped and resolves via task 012's Graph path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-049">Scope: any code in this task that reads, writes or repackages .docx bytes. ADR-049 governs the Compose .docx write path; read it before touching bytes. This task MUST NOT import from, extend, or share mutable state with `Services/Compose/**` or `Spaarke.Compose.Components` — the two write paths stay independent. If a shared OOXML helper looks tempting, escalate rather than coupling the spines.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: byte fidelity. Adding the custom XML part MUST NOT alter any other part of the package — body content, styles, numbering, section properties, relationships unrelated to the new part. Verify by round-tripping a fixture: stamp it, then confirm every pre-existing package part is byte-identical and the document opens cleanly in Word.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: non-.docx uploads. The save path also carries emails, attachments and other content types. The stamp applies ONLY where an OOXML package is present; a PDF, an EML or an arbitrary binary MUST pass through untouched, not fail and not be silently rewritten.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-044">Scope: the `sprk_document` GUID written into the stamp and every Dataverse GUID crossing a boundary here — canonicalize to bare lowercase via the shared `cleanGuid`. The stamped value must be the canonical form so the read side can match it without normalization ambiguity.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Scope: the upload path this task hooks. Graph SDK types stay behind `SpeFileStore`; the stamper operates on a byte stream, not on a Graph `DriveItem`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: BFF publish size. Measure the delta against a FRESH BUILD OF MASTER, not the recorded baseline (root CLAUDE.md §10 bullet 4). If an OOXML manipulation package is added, its size contribution is the dominant risk in this task — report it explicitly. Escalate at +5 MB or more; hard stop at 60 MB.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI registrations. Keep additions minimal. Prefer a method on an existing save-path service over a new registered service unless the stamper genuinely needs its own lifetime.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: pre-PR process. Run `/conflict-check` before opening the PR — `spaarkeai-compose-r8` owns the other .docx write path and is `parallel-safe:false` across the Compose spine.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: test obligation. A modified endpoint or save-path service requires contract/integration coverage. Banned: `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration tests, ctor null-check tests.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>OOXML custom XML parts, server-side byte stamping, save-path composition</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/spec.md</file>
