      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/content-identity-and-deduplication-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/office-outlook-teams-integration-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/COMPOSE-WRITE-RESIDUAL-LOSS.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-044-dataverse-guid-canonicalization.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="endpoint-definition" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md">If the stamp needs any route surface at all; prefer hooking the existing save path over adding a route.</pattern>
      <pattern name="endpoint-filters" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md">Authorization conventions if any new route is unavoidable.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load project CLAUDE.md (especially the Decisions table's forward-only entry), spec.md FR-02 and its Assumptions, plan.md §4 Phase 1, and ADR-049 in full. Declare: RIGOR LEVEL FULL, model-tier opus, effort high, steps mode DIRECTIONAL.</step>
    <step order="1">Trace the current save path from `POST /api/office/save` through `OfficeService.SaveAsync` to the point where .docx bytes are handed to storage. Identify the single place where the bytes are in memory AND the `sprk_document` GUID is known. Record it — if the GUID is not yet known at the byte-handoff point, that ordering problem is the real work of this task.</step>
    <step order="2">Decide the stamp's representation and record it in notes/ before implementing: the custom XML part's namespace, its root element, the GUID's canonical form, and how a reader distinguishes a Spaarke stamp from any other custom XML part in the package. Also decide whether additional fields (tenant, save timestamp) belong — default to the GUID alone unless a concrete consumer needs more (CLAUDE.md §11).</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the stamper: open the uploaded bytes as an OOXML package, add the custom XML part with its content-type entry and relationship, and repackage. Every pre-existing part must survive byte-identical. Non-OOXML payloads pass through untouched.</step>
    <step order="4">Hook the stamper into the save path at the point identified in step 1, ensuring the user's open document is never touched and the operation is idempotent — re-saving an already-stamped document updates or leaves the stamp coherent rather than accumulating duplicate parts.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement the read side: a stamped document's GUID is readable from the bytes so re-upload self-identifies WITHOUT a Graph round-trip. Wire it so identity resolution prefers the stamp and falls back to task 012's Graph path. Record the precedence in notes/.</step>
    <step order="6">Add integration coverage: stamp a fixture and assert all other parts byte-identical; assert the document opens in Word (or passes an OOXML validity check); assert a non-OOXML payload is unmodified; assert a pre-release unstamped document still resolves via the 012 path; assert re-saving does not duplicate the part.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` and `dotnet test`. Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`; confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE (especially relevant if an OOXML package was added).</step>
    <step order="8">Measure BFF publish size against a fresh build of master per the constraint; record both absolute sizes, the delta and the zip tool in notes/. Call out any package added for OOXML manipulation.</step>
    <step order="9">Run `/conflict-check` before opening the PR. State the Placement Justification per `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` in the PR description.</step>
    <step order="10">Update projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="11">Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/ — including the stamp representation, the precedence decision, and the byte-fidelity evidence.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If stamping cannot be done without altering other parts of the OOXML package (a repackage that rewrites unrelated parts, or a library that normalizes XML on save), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6. Silent byte churn on a user's work product is exactly the failure class ADR-049 was amended three times over — do not accept "the document still opens" as sufficient.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the `sprk_document` GUID is not available at the point in the save path where the bytes are handed to storage, and making it available would require reordering the save (create-record-before-upload), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — that reordering has dedup and idempotency consequences beyond this task's scope.</trigger>
    <trigger>If implementing the stamp appears to require sharing OOXML helper code with `Services/Compose/**`, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6.5 rather than coupling the two .docx write spines.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a scenario is found where forward-only stamping is insufficient and a retroactive rewrite seems necessary, STOP and escalate — the forward-only decision is an owner decision (2026-09-04), not an implementation default to be revisited in-task.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the publish-size delta is +5 MB or more against a fresh master build, STOP and escalate with explicit justification per root CLAUDE.md §10.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>None found for stamping. Grep of `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/**` for custom XML part handling (`customXml`, `CustomXmlPart`, `AddCustomXmlPart`) returns no stamp mechanism; spec.md's New Components table records the same conclusion ("Custom XML part stamper (server-side) — existing overlap: None"). The nearest neighbour is the Compose .docx write path under `Services/Compose/**` (ADR-049), which repackages document BODY content for an entirely different purpose and is explicitly out of bounds for coupling.</existing>
    <extension>No — the Compose write path is a body-content renderer governed by its own ADR with its own fidelity contract, and `spaarkeai-compose-r8` owns it as `parallel-safe:false`. Extending it would entangle two independent write spines and put this task's changes inside the Compose fidelity guarantees. The stamper is a small, additive package operation on the Office save path only.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A document that leaves Spaarke and comes back cannot be re-identified: a user who downloads a document, edits it locally, and re-uploads it through the pane creates a NEW `sprk_document` row on every round trip instead of a new version — because task 012's Graph path keys on the SPE item id, which a locally-saved copy no longer has. Every round trip permanently forks the record.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/`, test, publish (size measurement), `list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`</tool>
    <tool name="git">worktree add for the fresh master publish-size baseline</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeService.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/014-xml-part-stamp-decisions.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/014-publish-size.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a .docx saved through the Spaarke pane after this release, when the stored file is downloaded and its package inspected, then it contains a custom XML part carrying the canonical bare-lowercase `sprk_document` GUID.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given that downloaded stamped document, when it is re-uploaded through the pane, then it self-identifies to the original `sprk_document` WITHOUT a Graph round-trip.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a document saved BEFORE this release, when opened in the pane, then it is unaffected by this change and still resolves through task 012's Graph path — no stored bytes were rewritten.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the repo after this task, when searched for a backfill job, migration, or stamp-on-read path over existing documents, then none exists (forward-only, owner decision 2026-09-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the user's document open in Word during a Spaarke save, when the save completes, then the open document is NOT modified — Word does not report unsaved changes caused by Spaarke and does not prompt to save.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a fixture .docx, when stamped, then every pre-existing package part is byte-identical to the input and the resulting file opens cleanly in Word.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a non-OOXML payload (PDF, EML, arbitrary binary) on the same save path, when saved, then the bytes are passed through unmodified and no error is raised.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given an already-stamped document, when saved again, then the package contains exactly one Spaarke stamp part — parts do not accumulate.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a corrupt or truncated OOXML payload, when stamping is attempted, then it fails with a handled ProblemDetails error and does not write partial bytes to storage.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the new code, when inspected, then it does not import from `Services/Compose/**` or `Spaarke.Compose.Components` and shares no mutable state with the Compose write path (ADR-049 independence).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a publish of this branch and a fresh publish of `origin/master`, when both are zipped with PowerShell `Compress-Archive`, then the delta is recorded with both absolute sizes and the tool named, and is under +5 MB.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` succeeds, `dotnet test` passes, and `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` reports no new HIGH-severity CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`/conflict-check` was run before the PR and its result recorded; the PR description states the Placement Justification.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md FR-02, its Assumptions section, and Success Criterion 3 ("A stamped document, downloaded and re-opened from disk, self-identifies"). plan.md §4 Phase 1 task 014 and §7 risk R-5.
    The forward-only scope decision resolves spec.md's Unresolved Question at line 283 ("Backfill for FR-02"). It is an owner decision, recorded in project CLAUDE.md Decisions (2026-09-04) — treat it as binding, not as a default.
    Wave P1-b with task 015: 014 is server-side C# on `Services/Office/**` plus contract tests; 015 is client-side TypeScript/React in `shared/taskpane/**`. No shared file and no shared symbol — the pair is disjoint by construction.
  </notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
